c4 -- Connect Four==================    c4Play Connect Four against the computer on a lettered board.  The columnsare lettered a to g; type a column's letter to drop your piece down it.The first player to line up four or more in a row -- across, down or on adiagonal -- wins.  The program beeps when it threatens a winning move.Type `q' to quit and control-L to redraw the screen.Hard to beat, but it never learns.    G. L. Sicherman, comp.sources.games volume 12 issue 100, October 1991.    Posted to Usenet with no stated terms; carried here as it was posted.    Originals in SRC/conn4/ORIG.